# Every service builds with `context: .`, so without this the whole repo is
# uploaded to the daemon on every build -- including .env and secrets/, which
# hold real credentials, and .venv/, which is 80 MB of host-platform wheels
# that would be wrong inside the image anyway. No Dockerfile here COPYs the
# context wholesale, so nothing listed below was reaching an image; keeping it
# out of the context is about not handing credentials to the build at all, and
# about builds that do not re-upload a hundred megabytes to answer "did
# anything change".

# Credentials.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/

# Host virtualenv and caches. Wrong platform, and rebuilt inside the image.
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.uv-cache/

# History and tooling.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Data and operational output. `./data` is bind-mounted at runtime; baking a
# copy in would ship whatever personal data happened to be sitting in it.
data/
backups/
testfiles/

# Documentation and reports: nothing in an image reads these.
docs/
*.md
!README.md
pcdf-pipeline-blueprint.html
